ns3 provides ns-3's own CMake package, one target per module:

    find_package(ns3 CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE ns3::core ns3::internet ns3::wifi)

Headers as in an ns-3 tree: #include "ns3/core-module.h". They need C++23
(ns-3.49's minimum), which the targets do not set for you:

    target_compile_features(main PRIVATE cxx_std_23)

Shared libraries only (x64-linux). On ns-3.49 the port applies the upstream
fix for NS3-001 (stock AODV's ICMP no-route livelock, nsnam/ns-3-dev!3101),
so it is not stock ns-3 there: the org's images are. Known ns-3 bugs on this
release and the org's workarounds:
https://github.com/swarm-routing/sim-tools/blob/main/docs/ns3-bugs.md
